    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Description\n\nRelated discussion: https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/discussions/33#discussioncomment-10941958\r\n\r\nIt would be useful to allow filtering of files in `grep_live`. As per the discussion we have found a solution, but I still think this could be eventually builtin functionality. It could be done in several ways:\r\n- By introducing some functionality for filtering inside the picker, behaving similar to the `<C-Space>` keymap in `Pick files`\r\n- By allowing the modification of the command of pickers, either totally or by specifying specific arguments that the user can modify",
