    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nI was writing the justification for why this issue will be closed (the already explained \"too much to add\", there is a workaround, etc.), when decided to take an extra look just to be sure.\r\n\r\nOne of the problems here is that there are several tools available for `builtin.grep_live` (and `builtin.grep`, for that matter), and I thought 'git' tool does not support it. But it appears to indeed support that. And (by the initial looks of it) both tools can support this \"pre-filtering\" without huge amount of hassle.\r\n\r\nNow, the easiest way to add support for this kind of \"pre-filtering\" is to expose an extra local option. Something like `glob` which can then be used like `:Pick grep_live glob='*.ts'`. The downside here would be that it wouldn't be possible to change interactively.\r\n\r\nIt is possible to be added behind a special picker mapping, but I have doubts about a good default keys for that.\r\n\r\nI'll think about it.",
