            "body": "> Doing it at git level would make it work with all supported tools.\r\n\r\nThat's not *quite* what is meant here. Pattern search itself can be done either via `rg` or `git` CLI tools (with [these different commands](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/9618cf56e76cc0caab54ad60116a8d72f99d7b3b/lua/mini/pick.lua#L3259-L3269)). And ideally support for \"pre-filtering\" should be present in both.\r\n\r\nLuckily I have a working prototype which seems to work for both CLI tools and both `grep` / `grep_live`. It will need a period of manual testing and polishing, though.",
