        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Sorry, let me give you some more details...\r\n\r\n#### Things that changed in the `pick-glob` branch\r\n- It no longer respects my `.gitignore` (e.g. shows results inside `node_modules` directory)\r\n- My temporary rg config has a glob which just ignores anything inside the `.git` directory, it's not respecting that as well\r\n\r\n#### My setup\r\n- Temporary rg config (`$HOME/.config/nvim/.rg`):\r\n```\r\n--hidden\r\n--glob=!.git/\r\n--smart-case\r\n```\r\n- Relevant `mini.pick` config:\r\n```lua\r\n    local load_temp_rg = function(f)\r\n      local rg_env = 'RIPGREP_CONFIG_PATH'\r\n      local cached_rg_config = vim.uv.os_getenv(rg_env) or ''\r\n      vim.uv.os_setenv(rg_env, vim.fn.stdpath('config') .. '/.rg')\r\n      f()\r\n      vim.uv.os_setenv(rg_env, cached_rg_config)\r\n    end\r\n    \r\n    pick.registry.gl = function()\r\n      load_temp_rg(function()\r\n        pick.builtin.grep_live({ tool = 'rg' })\r\n      end)\r\n    end\r\n```\r\n- Call `:Pick gl`",
